From 0119d5daee9b8a07a8096331eea78dbbb6c26050 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@soprasteria.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 17:11:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Borg: judge Vampire Strike closeness on the chosen monster
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The closest-target scan left 'dist' holding the distance of the last
entry examined, including entries it skipped, so the 'relatively close'
guard rejected the strike whenever any single listed monster stood
twenty or more grids away — even with the chosen target close by.  Since
the chosen entry is the minimum, this only ever over-restricted the
spell.  Test the chosen distance (best_dist) instead.

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-fight-attack.c b/src/borg/borg-fight-attack.c
index 45c5d140a..c680602a3 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-fight-attack.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-fight-attack.c
@@ -3539,7 +3539,7 @@ static int borg_attack_aux_vampire_strike(void)
         return 0;
 
     /* Nothing to attack, require relatively close */
-    if (dist >= 20)
+    if (best_dist >= 20)
         return 0;
 
     x = borg_temp_x[b_i];
